# GCE budget kill switch (auto-stop at EUR 10)

Invoke with `@gce-budget-kill`. **Agent runs terminal via Shell.**

**Goal:** When monthly spend exceeds the EUR 10 budget, automatically stop `vst-vela-01`.

**Judgment:** `.cursor/skills/gce-ops/SKILL.md`

| Name | Value |
| :--- | :--- |
| Budget | `pt-vela` (EUR 10/month) |
| Budget ID | `41e9b2e3-229a-4663-bb8c-40db5d00bbe9` |
| Pub/Sub topic | `pt-vela-budget-alerts` |
| Cloud Function | `pt-vela-budget-stop-vm` |

---

## One-time setup

From repo root on **Mac**:

```sh
chmod +x scripts/gce_vela/budget_kill_switch/setup.sh
scripts/gce_vela/budget_kill_switch/setup.sh
```

**Pass:** setup prints budget `notificationsRule` with Pub/Sub topic; function deploy succeeds.

---

## Limits

| Limit | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| Not instant | Pub/Sub budget messages can lag billing by hours |
| Alerts only until setup | Budget emails do not stop VMs by themselves |
| Scope | Stops `vst-vela-01` only when `costAmount > budgetAmount` |
| Disk + GCS | Still bill when VM is TERMINATED |

Always use `@gce-stop` after VELA work; kill switch is a safety net.

